mori::syntax::decimal_without_asset

  × A decimal number needs an asset.
   ╭─[test.mori:3:16]
 2 │ agreement Invoice {
 3 │   const rate = 1.5;
   ·                ─┬─
   ·                 ╰── which asset is this an amount of?
 4 │ }
   ╰────
  help: Decimals are only allowed for amounts, because the asset decides how
        many decimal places are valid. Name the asset, or use a whole number:

            const rate = 1.5 USD;
